{
  "$comment": [
    "What a person reads for a catalog model: cleanModelName(id, display_name, provider), without the route the gateway takes to it.",
    "Neuron never shows the provider a model is routed through (Groq, OpenRouter, NVIDIA, Z.ai, ...), so every copy of the cleaner has to give these answers:",
    "  ui/neuron-client/src/copy/model-name.ts           (the shared client: desktop and mobile)",
    "  ui/neuron-tui/src/utils/model-name.ts             (the full-screen terminal UI)",
    "  rust/crates/rusty-claude-cli/src/gateway_catalog.rs  (clean_model_name: the engine's own notices, status and JSON output)",
    "Each one's tests read this file, so they cannot drift apart. Change a rule here and in all three.",
    "",
    "sections[].cases: [id, display_name, provider, expected]. null is 'not given'; an empty string is given and empty.",
    "providerShapes: for every provider P, every form of it (P, P in lower case, P in upper case), every bracket and every gap,",
    "  the name is 'Model' + gap + open + form + close, and what is read is 'Model'.",
    "joinedRoutes: the name is 'Model (Groq' + joiner + extra + ')'; one part, so every word of it is a route word, and what is read is 'Model'.",
    "separatedRoutes: the name is 'Model (Groq' + separator + extra + ')'; two parts, each judged alone: [extra, what is read].",
    "All of them are cleaned with id 'x/model' and no provider, unless a case says otherwise."
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "name": "the route the gateway takes to the model is left out",
      "cases": [
        ["cohere/north-mini-code:free", "North Mini Code (OpenRouter, free)", "openrouter", "North Mini Code"],
